<component type="desktop-application">
  <id>io.github.naoomeow.Pointerctl</id>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT</project_license>
  <name>Pointerctl</name>
  <developer id="io.github.naoomeow"><name>pointerctl contributors</name></developer>
  <summary>Unofficial settings tool for mice</summary>
  <description>
    <p>Change the settings stored on a mouse without the manufacturer's Windows software: DPI levels, polling rate, button debounce time, button functions (including keyboard shortcuts and media keys) and lighting.</p>
    <p>Currently supports the Meetion GM21. Other models are not tested yet and are refused unless you explicitly override the check. This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by Meetion.</p>
    <p>The mouse needs a one-time udev rule so your user can access it. The package installs it; with Flatpak, run the installer script from the project page once.</p>
  </description>
  <launchable type="desktop-id">io.github.naoomeow.Pointerctl.desktop</launchable>
  <url type="homepage">https://github.com/naOomeow/pointerctl</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/naOomeow/pointerctl/issues</url>
  <provides><binary>pointerctl-gui</binary><binary>pointerctl</binary></provides>
  <categories><category>Settings</category><category>HardwareSettings</category></categories>
  <content_rating type="oars-1.1"/>
